1
00:04:28,571 --> 00:04:34,571
You'll laugh. You'll cry. You'll hurl.

2
00:08:57,142 --> 00:09:03,142
Wayne's World is a comedy, music film directed by Penelope Spheeris.

3
00:13:25,714 --> 00:13:31,714
The adventures of two amiably aimless metal-head friends, Wayne and Garth.

4
00:17:54,285 --> 00:18:00,285
From Wayne's basement, the pair broadcast a talk-show called
"Wayne's World" on local public access television.

5
00:22:22,857 --> 00:22:28,857
The show comes to the attention of a sleazy network executive who wants to produce a big-budget version
of "Wayne's World"—and he also wants Wayne's girlfriend, a rock singer named Cassandra.

6
00:26:51,428 --> 00:26:57,428
Wayne and Garth have to battle the executive not only
to save their show, but also Cassandra.

7
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Wayne Campbell, played by Mike Myers.

8
00:35:48,571 --> 00:35:54,571
Garth Algar, played by Dana Carvey.

9
00:40:17,142 --> 00:40:23,142
Benjamin Kane, played by Rob Lowe.

10
00:44:45,714 --> 00:44:51,714
Cassandra, played by Tia Carrere.

11
00:49:14,285 --> 00:49:20,285
Stacy, played by Lara Flynn Boyle.

12
00:53:42,857 --> 00:53:48,857
Dreamwoman, played by Donna Dixon.

13
00:58:11,428 --> 00:58:17,428
Wayne's World is a 1992 American comedy film directed by Penelope Spheeris, produced by
Lorne Michaels, and written by Mike Myers and Bonnie and Terry Turner.

14
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Based on the SNL sketch by Myers, it stars Myers in his feature film debut as Wayne Campbell and Dana Carvey as
Garth Algar, a pair of rock and heavy metal fans who broadcast a public-access television show.

15
01:07:08,571 --> 01:07:14,571
It also features Tia Carrere, Rob Lowe, Lara Flynn Boyle and Brian Doyle-Murray in supporting roles, with
cameos by Chris Farley, Ed O'Neill, Ione Skye, Meat Loaf, Robert Patrick and Alice Cooper.

16
01:11:37,142 --> 01:11:43,142
Wayne's World was released in the United States on
February 14, 1992, by Paramount Pictures.

17
01:16:05,714 --> 01:16:11,714
A critical and commercial success, it was the tenth-highest-grossing film of 1992 and
remains the highest-grossing film based on a Saturday Night Live sketch.

18
01:20:34,285 --> 01:20:40,285
A sequel, Wayne's World 2, was released the following year.

19
01:25:02,857 --> 01:25:08,857
The film explores themes of romantic rivalry, heavy metal,
parody, singer, breaking the fourth wall.

20
01:29:31,428 --> 01:29:37,428
The tone is lighthearted.
